notice('These draft rules describe a possible future operation. Rights and fishing access are not confirmed. They do not grant permission to visit or fish.');
echo '<section class="panel"><h2>Care for the water. Respect the place.</h2><ul><li>Fish only when the project has confirmed it is open, on your booked date and within published operating hours.</li><li>One ticket per angler. Show your QR ticket to authorised staff. Tickets are checked in once.</li><li>Follow bailiff instructions, respect neighbours and other visitors, and keep noise low. No night fishing.</li><li>Use barbless hooks, a suitable landing net and an unhooking mat. Handle fish carefully and return them promptly. No removal, introduction or transfer of fish.</li><li>Do not leave rods unattended. Take all litter, line and hooks home. No fires, swimming or unauthorised work.</li><li>Children must be supervised by a responsible adult. Stay away from unsafe banks and wildlife-sensitive areas.</li><li>Hold any rod licence required for your fishing. A site ticket does not replace a rod licence.</li></ul><h3>Before bookings open</h3><p>The organiser must finalise opening hours, rod and bait limits, accessibility information, emergency arrangements and cancellation terms, and update this page. Current sample prices are not an offer of access.</p><h3>Booking changes and refunds</h3><p>Contact the organiser before your fishing date to request a change or cancellation. Do not purchase another ticket to correct an existing booking. If the organiser cancels a fishing day, affected paid bookings should be refunded. Refunds are processed through the original payment provider; your ticket page shows the recorded status.</p></section>'; foot();
